# This repo is public and its folders publish, so their keys sit beside the content.
# Each folder's own .moss/.gitignore, written by moss, already ignores the key;
# these lines repeat it so a folder missing that file still cannot leak one.
**/.moss/identity/
**/.moss/keys/
# moss tracks these two on purpose, as facts about the site; here they would point
# someone who takes a folder at our address. Delete once moss handles a folder
# whose publish target belongs to another account.
**/.moss/state.toml
**/.moss/deploy/
.worktrees/
.DS_Store
